Give camera_info the same frame_id as the TF tree and the image.

generate_cam_info() sets header.frame_id to "<camera>_optical", while the static TF and the
image both use "<vehicle>/<camera>_optical". image_proc, depth_image_proc and any TF-aware
perception node therefore cannot resolve the camera frame.

Measured (drone-sim, 2026-08-02, vehicle "PX4"):

    camera_info frame_id : front_center_optical
    image       frame_id : PX4/front_center_optical
    tf_static child      : PX4/front_center_optical

Both the Scene and DepthPlanar camera_info topics are affected.

generate_cam_info() used camera_name only for this frame_id, so this threads the vehicle name
through explicitly rather than passing a pre-prefixed string under a "camera_name" argument --
the call sites already have curr_vehicle_name in scope (declared at airsim_ros_wrapper.cpp:165).

This is an upstream defect and is worth reporting to Cosys-Lab.

NOTE ON LINE ENDINGS: Cosys-AirSim sources are CRLF. This hunk was GENERATED from the real
files, not hand-written -- a hand-written LF hunk fails with
"Hunk 1 FAILED (different line endings)".

